From fedbead493b0789ba575828e4eb43b6f9f4cf7e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joris OFFOUGA <offougajoris@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:06:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] plat-imx: add i.MX8MP Cortex-M7 remoteproc support

Let the remoteproc TA authenticate, load, start and stop the i.MX8MP
Cortex-M7 firmware, for Linux imx_rproc "fsl,imx8mp-cm7-tee".

The driver holds the M7 memory map (ITCM, DTCM and an optional DDR region
set with CFG_IMX_REMOTEPROC_DDR_START/SIZE) and the start/stop sequences of
the TF-A IMX_SIP_SRC service: start clears IOMUXC_GPR22 CM7_CPUWAIT; stop
requests the GPC sleep hold, sets CPUWAIT back and resets the M7 core and
platform through SRC_M7RCR.

The PTA is the STM32MP one on top of this driver, with the
PTA_RPROC_SET_MEMORY fill value fixed (bitwise instead of logical AND).

Enable with CFG_IMX_REMOTEPROC=y: it embeds the remoteproc early TA and the
public part of RPROC_SIGN_KEY, used to verify the firmware signature
(scripts/sign_rproc_fw.py).

The M7 is a non-secure bus master and its TCMs are accessible from the
normal world: the firmware is authenticated when loaded, not protected
afterwards.

Signed-off-by: Joris OFFOUGA <offougajoris@icloud.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/plat-imx/conf.mk           |  18 ++
 core/drivers/remoteproc/imx_remoteproc.c | 267 ++++++++++++++++
 core/drivers/remoteproc/sub.mk           |   1 +
 core/include/drivers/imx_remoteproc.h    |  71 +++++
 core/pta/imx/remoteproc_pta.c            | 371 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 core/pta/imx/rproc_pub_key.h             |  16 +
 core/pta/imx/sub.mk                      |   1 +
 7 files changed, 745 insertions(+)
